WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.550
Before anyone decides anything, count.

2
00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:07.651
Twenty years of growth leave three kinds
of sprawl: more instances than anyone

3
00:00:07.651 --> 00:00:12.988
remembers, databases nobody can account
for, and dependencies that cross domains.

4
00:00:12.988 --> 00:00:17.458
No single tool finds them all, so
the program combines a network sweep,

5
00:00:17.458 --> 00:00:20.673
the Kerberos registration
trail and Microsoft's

6
00:00:20.673 --> 00:00:23.888
assessment tools into one
inventory it can re-run.

7
00:00:23.888 --> 00:00:26.175
The book's illustration makes the point.

8
00:00:26.175 --> 00:00:28.927
A team that believes it
has forty instances,

9
00:00:28.927 --> 00:00:32.750
when discovery finds a hundred
and ten, isn't behind schedule.

10
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.962
Its whole estimate is wrong
by nearly three times.

11
00:00:35.962 --> 00:00:40.462
Missing instances surface at the worst
possible moment unless you look first.

12
00:00:40.462 --> 00:00:42.380
Then each one needs a verdict.
